api.github.com/users/Xiexe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T10:32:05Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T10:36:21Z","body":"> Is the shader code based on the description of the process in the talk or is it taken from some example code?\r\n\r\nCode is from https://github.com/dmnsgn/glsl-tone-map/blob/main/lottes.glsl which I can only assume is an accurate representation of tone mapper based on the talk. Aside from the GDC talk and this one specific repo with an implementation of it, there's not really a lot of mention of it anywhere that I've been able to find.\r\n\r\nI have not watched the full talk, but there is mention of there being code in the slides.\r\n\r\nAlso, apparently the code in the slides was flawed in some way, and the corrected version can be found [here](https://bartwronski.com/2016/09/01/dynamic-range-and-evs/) in the comments (at the very bottom).. which looks to be accurate to what's happening in this version.\r\n\r\nAlso, HDR_MAX is apparently the white point, so may want to expose that as a parameter again. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3244746461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/324476