vatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5119787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe","html_url":"https://github.com/Xiexe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xiexe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T11:18:43Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T11:18:43Z","body":"> But the code you copied is under the MIT license, that's what needs to be cited, unless it is identical to the slides, in which case we'd need to know what license that is under\r\n\r\nIt's pretty close to the slides. Ill add an attribute to the git repo and keep the attribute to the GDC talk tomorrow.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3244900270/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246078409","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110190#issuecomment-3246078409","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110190","id":3246078409,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BeznJ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T16:46:16Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T16:46:44Z","body":"Thanks for opening a pull request :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\nFeature pull requests should be associated to a *feature proposal* to justify the need for implementing the feature in Godot core. Please open a proposal on the [Godot proposals](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals) repository (and link to this pull request in the proposal's body).\r\n\r\nAlso, is this tonemapper friendly to [HDR output](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94496)? To me, if we're going to add yet another tonemapper in Godot, it ought to be HDR-friendly from the ground up. cc @allenwp","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246078409/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246128675","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110190#issuecomment-3246128675","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110190","id":3246128675,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Be_4j","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T17:03:47Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T22:14:39Z","body":"That's a really great talk that Timothy Lottes presented at GDC 2016 -- I learned a lot from it! Unfortunately, although this tone curve was advertised as working well with \"variable dynamic range\", it is actually quite unstable. So I spent a fair bit of time iterating on this approach that Timothy presented and [developed a tonemapping curve that is better suited](https://allenwp.com/blog/2025/05/29/allenwp-tonemapping-curve/) for the variable \"Extended Dynamic Range\" (EDR) that [Godot will be adopting for HDR output](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94496).\r\n\r\nI made a work in progress prototype that implements this curve as the \"Adjustable\" tonemapping curve in this draft PR here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106696 -- The goal of this is to add an adjustable replacement to the \"Filmic\" tonemapper that works well with EDR/HDR, because \"Filmic\" simply cannot work with HDR because of its \"white\" parameter implementation. I want to spend more time ensuring that the \"black\" parameter works well with it before making a final PR, though...\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I have made an update to the AgX tonemapper that uses this new EDR-stable tonemapping curve, slightly modified to better suit the intent of AgX: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106940","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3246128675/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]